-6ca2-5422-a4d7-a1ad6f5a67f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-65166" :question/problem "What is $\\frac{\\sin^{2} x}{\\sin^{3} x + \\sin x\\cos^{2} x}$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e29407f-0306-5cd7-ab50-d46e971435f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251071} {:answer/id #uuid "6218e58c-9107-5231-b02a-3a84de60083e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251349} {:answer/id #uuid "ae27a1dd-2895-5936-945a-8057f5eb72ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252071} {:answer/id #uuid "d57697f1-9470-5638-87e8-1592607aa161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252444} {:answer/id #uuid "f07f9d80-b3ae-5297-8430-2159434cec87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae27a1dd-2895-5936-945a-8057f5eb72ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252071} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad77e15e-6b7f-5b66-be54-92af8304ca70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253106}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f206d2c2-ee8e-56e4-8de0-ea23491335cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-119379" :question/problem "$\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0decdc0f-4b98-5c65-a3b0-d86ae94d22ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250673} {:answer/id #uuid "179fe940-7b73-5546-bf32-fed03990fd82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250762} {:answer/id #uuid "1b8d6af1-4d22-5cfb-b898-7e256d885ca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250789} {:answer/id #uuid "3475e5a6-689a-521d-b598-8eb44369e318" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250988} {:answer/id #uuid "6287be61-1f4d-505f-b9e8-81ea18208894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "179fe940-7b73-5546-bf32-fed03990fd82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250762} :answer-field/id #uuid "154c7544-e9aa-5942-a1f1-f550a4df2949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252847}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7483895f-9f2e-5510-9cf9-357e34d2424a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119381" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta .\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ed664b-fff1-5712-ac2e-5525f9cdacef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250634} {:answer/id #uuid "3b69e247-6d23-5ff1-a976-eb6503b80dcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251045} {:answer/id #uuid "58c39cbe-5a9b-575c-ae8a-d7f92d34e4dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251282} {:answer/id #uuid "923c3e09-f2e0-5124-82ce-83280737e8aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251804} {:answer/id #uuid "b061ebd1-c842-5f84-80fa-eec468f6b43d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08ed664b-fff1-5712-ac2e-5525f9cdacef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250634} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a2bbe3-2ba2-5a56-9f75-7bcd2efd08bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253041}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e604df29-4056-5a18-af72-ee9756feedd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-119387" :question/problem "$\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "103f5b2e-5c31-5097-a363-9f6afaafdbb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250694} {:answer/id #uuid "4b13d84e-fa74-5321-92fd-9d3ab8999d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251178} {:answer/id #uuid "53ddef33-f78b-53ce-9fde-d6f939e3fb9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251239} {:answer/id #uuid "a784c34d-c4aa-591d-a102-942798280f5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251996} {:answer/id #uuid "da6b22ed-a42d-50cf-92ea-c1fdfd820128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53ddef33-f78b-53ce-9fde-d6f939e3fb9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251239} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15dbfd9-4666-5a0a-a3af-8408df3d5a73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253227}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c41ec619-a5e7-5d9c-af90-cb7a886021e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119392" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ from the first two terms of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot 1+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a40e44-d0af-5c89-b80a-3396d5a21c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333168} {:answer/id #uuid "750bdb38-76dc-5921-b853-233af7a4114b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334045} {:answer/id #uuid "83ab2b2f-ab51-55f5-b8c7-4ed8ed555c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334162} {:answer/id #uuid "ef01b601-79a0-57a1-8aea-e6b0580bb0a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335086} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5fceb5-1b21-51bc-b719-72691e076949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83ab2b2f-ab51-55f5-b8c7-4ed8ed555c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334162} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc929786-96c0-5afd-8709-2af6ff4df9db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335679}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "408e1d81-b8ca-526c-9d23-4441a1e9e3da" :question/math-academy-id "q-65246" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1658712a-8ba1-59c8-827d-6896d0c4a89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333189} {:answer/id #uuid "51f35fc5-f8b5-52c5-bd72-f5ee50de7ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333740} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc73464-ee87-5565-b343-67b1427f2f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333836} {:answer/id #uuid "9cca540c-e544-5aad-8198-91ff220acbb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334367} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a51e1a-29dd-58ab-bde9-9549015dc84a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1a51e1a-29dd-58ab-bde9-9549015dc84a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335108} :answer-field/id #uuid "30de960e-761f-5b8d-8824-72cc0644a704" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335335}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ed4d5cd-bcc7-5b6f-b453-67face29d90e" :question/math-academy-id "q-65248" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1567a263-7b89-55fb-bfa3-dd6519d37da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333179} {:answer/id #uuid "1efadbf7-3fd0-515a-bd3e-2f0e38a3c1b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333263} {:answer/id #uuid "44ac129e-ff18-5ebe-8e6b-31f66950fb8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333624} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9cf272-f6d5-5887-ad63-ad0fe82ecdf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333825} {:answer/id #uuid "c060f9dc-3224-5a52-90ca-da0bc7261a71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c060f9dc-3224-5a52-90ca-da0bc7261a71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334657} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a06711a-072f-51a1-b0cf-d4ac57f270d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335286}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae64dc03-6947-569b-9195-231675eb4838" :question/math-academy-id "q-65249" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d5cf9e-61a5-56dc-ab85-48cc3361b6cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339348} {:answer/id #uuid "2a4a8bfb-24ab-5d4f-85c0-b03c7be1078c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339502} {:answer/id #uuid "5af65e91-2dda-5a02-a6b9-84e591e12cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339956} {:answer/id #uuid "94adee08-1ae4-5711-87c2-0b92afcedb4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340463} {:answer/id #uuid "a2128603-79a4-5ac2-aad8-d0e79ce06174" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94adee08-1ae4-5711-87c2-0b92afcedb4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340463} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ffbbed8-ad51-5238-b319-cf240d8126f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341605}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "508dcfe6-ec7a-5fa0-ab23-63e62cd88ad5" :question/math-academy-id "q-72712" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d962943-db75-5bbc-9aa3-6b784b3c37c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(8\\cdot\\left(\\csc \\theta\\right))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543907} {:answer/id #uuid "2c20249b-7432-5b5b-93c8-728d6bf3ab6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(8\\cdot\\left(\\csc \\theta\\right))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543916} {:answer/id #uuid "3b93c5df-fd4d-5d4e-9532-11976ee37256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\cdot\\left(\\sin \\theta\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543922} {:answer/id #uuid "6bfda229-e5b8-545c-9faf-e2cbe587225e" :answer/type {:db