\operatorname{sec}⁡\\phi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543927} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4bb8f7-e950-572d-b909-b7691078d5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "694d3240-f1c3-5bf9-b1d0-e579178b1749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\phi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543927} :answer-field/id #uuid "97abb51b-60dd-5d8a-87cc-8deda195a885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543939}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f4a5275a-4ac6-5cc3-ad58-4b1c9fb73487" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡\\phi +{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi {cos}^{2}⁡\\phi +{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡\\phi +{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi {cos}^{2}⁡\\phi +{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right)=2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi ({sin}^{2}⁡\\phi +{cos}^{2}⁡\\phi )+{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right)\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi ({sin}^{2}⁡\\phi +{cos}^{2}⁡\\phi )+{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right) & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\cdot 1+{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\phi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡\\phi +{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi {cos}^{2}⁡\\phi +{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi }{{sin}^{2}⁡\\phi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi }\\right)=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\phi.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"}]}
